    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0998" n="902" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg902"/>

                <head>No. 412.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moran to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 1, 1879</date>.
                        (Received May 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 255.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the receipt of your No. 134, I addressed
                    a note in the sense thereof to Mr. Corvo, a copy of which I inclose, expressing
                    the satisfaction of the Government of the United States with the action of the
                    governor-general of the Cape Verde Islands in providing a new cemetery for the
                    remains of the Americans now lying in the old naval cemetery <pb facs="0999"
                        n="903" xml:id="pg903"/> there, and requested that information of these
                    sentiments of his kindness may be officially communicated to the
                    governor-general in question.</p>
                <p>My note was addressed to Mr. Corvo on the 4th of March. But should one come I
                    will immediately forward a copy.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>BENJAMIN MORAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
